{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"restful-cerebellar-mouse","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context\nThe RCA for broadish-permanent-condor found seven additional `@pytest.fixture` functions that return a full `dict(os.environ)` directly or nested inside the fixture argument pytest renders. Default long tracebacks can print early ambient credentials through `saferepr`. Confirmed fixtures: `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_materialize_probe.py`, `test_autodeploy_fetch_secrets.py`, `test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py`, `test_autodeploy_health_gate.py`, `test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py`, `test_observability_exit.py`, and `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py`.\n\nThe scope boundary is the decorated pytest-fixture return path. An AST sweep found no eighth fixture. In particular, `test_autodeploy_materialize_certbot.py::_make_box` is a plain helper whose result is assigned to a test local, so an unrelated later assertion does not render it as a fixture argument; a runtime long/short traceback probe confirmed the sentinel stays absent. A distinct exception-time carrier exists for 103 test-local subprocess mappings when the subprocess call itself raises; follow-up `antiutopic-toadyish-goldfinch` owns that larger audit. Runtime/maintenance environment propagation is excluded because preserving caller credentials/config is a separate product contract.\n\n## Plan\n- Build a parametrized real-pytest RED oracle using insertion-ordered synthetic sentinels and deterministic unrelated failures for each of the seven decorated fixture surfaces.\n- Replace each broad ambient copy with an explicit mutable allowlist: fake-bin-first `PATH` plus that harness's declared variables and per-test overrides. This is preferred over a representation wrapper because the subprocess contract itself should be explicit, the 24-test minimal-parent-environment run proves arbitrary keys are unnecessary, and it avoids adding a shared abstraction solely for test fixtures.\n- Prove sentinel absence under default long traceback and preserve the short-traceback negative control.\n- Run every existing fixture consumer under the minimal parent environment and the normal focused suites.\n- Reintroduce the exact broad-copy mutation and require the oracle to return to RED.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Each of the seven decorated fixtures has a deterministic RED failure-rendering probe.\n- [x] No decorated fixture in the AST construct sweep returns arbitrary ambient values.\n- [x] Default long traceback output contains no synthetic ambient sentinel on any of the seven surfaces.\n- [x] The fake-bin-first `PATH` remains available to every existing fixture consumer.\n- [x] Explicit harness environment variables remain mutable by their existing tests.\n- [x] [operator-attested] The 24-test minimal-parent-environment suite passes.\n  provenance: environment=minimal-parent-worktree-aa41c2e45a; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — 42-pass real pytest fixture/subprocess run under env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin\n- [x] [operator-attested] Focused suites pass.\n  provenance: environment=minimal-parent-worktree-aa41c2e45a; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — affected real fixture consumers plus held-out rendering oracle\n- [x] [operator-attested] Lint passes.\n  provenance: environment=gerrit-ci-run-32111971923; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — canonical gating Ruff, formatting, and repository policy checks\n- [x] [operator-attested] Typecheck passes.\n  provenance: environment=gerrit-ci-run-32111971923; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — canonical gating mypy run\n- [x] The exact broad-copy mutation returns the security oracle to RED.","id":"107a-307f-f2d9-4332","parent_id":"4ace-472a-01a7-40bd","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Prevent sibling pytest fixtures from rendering ambient credentials"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788233670116227001,"uuid":"e3d6fc49-d531-49fd-98a1-2b2983204296"}